[541.885954, "o", "0Hfter all tests finished?\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;215m\u001b[21;60Hdemo $ \u001b[39m# All 73 serialisation tests and 6 of 7 integration tests pass; see the article for the one failure.\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;215m\u001b[22;60Hdemo $ \u001b[39mcd .. && git clone -q --depth 1 --branch v2.7.0 https://github.com/michaelwittig/node-q.git\u001b[K\u001b[23;60HNote: switching to '17641112da5296c3c7920de26dc23d8cba73fcf9'.\u001b[K\u001b[24;60H\u001b[K\nYou are in 'detached HEAD' state. You can look around, make experimental\u001b[K\u001b[26;60Hchanges and commit them, and you can discard any commits you make in this\u001b[K\u001b[27;60Hstate without impacting any branches by switching back to a branch.\u001b[K\u001b[28;60H\u001b[K\nIf you want to create a new branch to retain commits you create, you may\u001b[K\u001b[30;60Hdo so (now or later) by using -c with the switch command. Example:\u001b[K\u001b[31;60H\u001b[K\n  git switch -c <new-branch-name>\u001b[K\u001b[33;60H\u001b[K\nOr undo this operation with:\u001b[K\u001b[35;60H\u001b[K\n  git switch -\u001b[K\u001b[37;60H\u001b[K\nTurn off this advice by setting config variable advice.detachedHead to false\u001b[K\u001b[39;60H\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;215m\ndemo $ \u001b[39mmkdi"]
