[550.39087, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[2m\u001b[2dRan all test suites matching \u001b(B\u001b[mintegration\u001b[2m.\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[1m\u001b[3;60HForce exiting Jest: \u001b(B\u001b[mHave you considered using `--detectOpenHandles` to detect async operations that kept running a\u001b[4;60Hfter all tests finished?\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;215m\u001b[5;60Hdemo $ \u001b[39m# All 73 serialisation tests and 6 of 7 integration tests pass; see the article for the one failure.\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;215m\u001b[6;60Hdemo $ \u001b[39mcd .. && git clone -q --depth 1 --branch v2.7.0 https://github.com/michaelwittig/node-q.git\u001b[K\u001b[7;60HNote: switching to '17641112da5296c3c7920de26dc23d8cba73fcf9'.\u001b[K\u001b[8;60H\u001b[K\nYou are in 'detached HEAD' state. You can look around, make experimental\u001b[K\u001b[10;60Hchanges and commit them, and you can discard any commits you make in this\u001b[K\u001b[11;60Hstate without impacting any branches by switching back to a branch.\u001b[K\u001b[12;60H\u001b[K\nIf you want to create a new branch to retain commits you create, you may\u001b[K\u001b[14;60Hdo so (now or later) by using -c with the switch command. Example:\u001b[K\u001b[15;60H\u001b[K\n  git switch -c <new-branch-name"]
