[550.617295, "o", "d and tested way to coalesce async requests by a key value, which is much more comprehensive\u001b[35;60H and powerful.\u001b[K\u001b[1m\u001b[36;60Hnpm\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[33mwarn\u001b[39m \u001b[94mdeprecated\u001b[39m graceful-fs@2.0.3: please upgrade to graceful-fs 4 for compatibility with current and future v\u001b[37;60Hersions of Node.js\u001b[K\u001b[1m\u001b[38;60Hnpm\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[33mwarn\u001b[39m \u001b[94mdeprecated\u001b[39m glob@5.0.15: Old versions of glob are not supported, and contain widely publicized security vu\u001b[39;60Hlnerabilities, which have been fixed in the current version. Please update. Support for old versions may be purcha\u001b[40;60Hsed (at exorbitant rates) by contacting i@izs.me\u001b[K\u001b[1m\u001b[41;60Hnpm\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[33mwarn\u001b[39m \u001b[94mdeprecated\u001b[39m are-we-there-yet@1.1.5: This package is no longer supported.\u001b[K\u001b[1m\u001b[42;60Hnpm\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[33mwarn\u001b[39m \u001b[94mdeprecated\u001b[39m gauge@2.7.4: This package is no longer supported.\u001b[K\u001b[1m\u001b[43;60Hnpm\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[33mwarn\u001b[39m \u001b[94mdeprecated\u001b[39m q@1.1.2: You or someone you depend on is using Q, the JavaScript Promise library that gave Jav\u001b[44;60HaS"]
[550.617305, "o", "cript developers strong feelings about promises. They can almost certainly migrate to the native JavaScript prom\u001b[45;60Hise now. Thank you literally everyone for joining me in this bet against the odds. Be excellent to each other.\u001b[K\u001b[1m\u001b[46;60Hnpm\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[33mwarn\u001b[39m \u001b[94mdeprecated\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[1m\u001b[47;60Hnpm\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[33mwarn\u001b[39m \u001b[94mdeprecated\u001b[39m (For a CapTP with native promises, see @endo/eventual-send and @endo/captp)\u001b[K\u001b[48;60H\u001b[K\u001b[?12l\u001b[?25h"]
[550.618346, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[2dstate without impacting any branches by switching back to a branch.\u001b[K\u001b[3;60H\u001b[K\nIf you want to create a new branch to retain commits you create, you may\u001b[K\u001b[5;60Hdo so (now or later) by using -c with the switch command. Example:\u001b[K\u001b[6;60H\u001b[K\n  git switch -c <new-branch-name>\u001b[K\u001b[8;60H\u001b[K\nOr undo this operation with:\u001b[K\u001b[10;60H\u001b[K\n  git switch -\u001b[K\u001b[12;60H\u001b[K\nTurn off this advice by setting config variable advice.detachedHead to false\u001b[K\u001b[14;60H\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;215m\ndemo $ \u001b[39mmkdir -p tick && curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/KxSystems/kdb-tick/master/tick/u.q -o tick/u.\u001b[16;60Hq && ls tick\u001b[K\u001b[17;60Hu.q\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;215m\u001b[18;60Hdemo $ \u001b[39mopenssl req -x509 -newkey rsa:2048 -nodes -subj /CN=localhost -keyout key.pem -out cert.pem -days 1 2>/dev/\u001b[19;60Hnull\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;215m\u001b[20;60Hdemo $ \u001b[39mSSL_CERT_FILE=$PWD/cert.pem SSL_KEY_FILE=$PWD/key.pem ./peachq/q -p 6000 -E 2 -q </dev/null >tls.log 2>&1 &\u001b[21;60H[1] 415816\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;215m\u001b[22;60Hdemo $ \u001b[39mcd node-q && npm install\u001b[K\u001b[1m\u001b[23;60Hnpm\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b["]
[550.618453, "o", "33mwarn\u001b[39m \u001b[94mold lockfile\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[1m\u001b[24;60Hnpm\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[33mwarn\u001b[39m \u001b[94mold lockfile\u001b[39m The package-lock.json file was created with an old version of npm,\u001b[K\u001b[1m\u001b[25;60Hnpm\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[33mwarn\u001b[39m \u001b[94mold lockfile\u001b[39m so supplemental metadata must be fetched from the registry.\u001b[K\u001b[1m\u001b[26;60Hnpm\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[33mwarn\u001b[39m \u001b[94mold lockfile\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[1m\u001b[27;60Hnpm\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[33mwarn\u001b[39m \u001b[94mold lockfile\u001b[39m This is a one-time fix-up, please be patient...\u001b[K\u001b[1m\u001b[28;60Hnpm\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[33mwarn\u001b[39m \u001b[94mold lockfile\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[1m\u001b[29;60Hnpm\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[33mwarn\u001b[39m \u001b[94mdeprecated\u001b[39m minimatch@2.0.10: Please update to minimatch 3.0.2 or higher to avoid a RegExp DoS issue\u001b[K\u001b[1m\u001b[30;60Hnpm\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[33mwarn\u001b[39m \u001b[94mdeprecated\u001b[39m inflight@1.0.6: This module is not supported, and leaks memory. Do not use it. Check out lru-c\u001b[31;60Hache if you want a good and tested way to coalesce async requests by a key value, which is much more comprehensive\u001b[32;60H and powerful.\u001b[K\u001b[1m\u001b[33;60Hnpm\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[33mwarn\u001b[39m \u001b[94mdeprecated\u001b"]
