[550.618799, "o", "ted.\u001b[K\u001b[1m\u001b[36;60Hnpm\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[33mwarn\u001b[39m \u001b[94mdeprecated\u001b[39m gauge@2.7.4: This package is no longer supported.\u001b[K\u001b[1m\u001b[37;60Hnpm\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[33mwarn\u001b[39m \u001b[94mdeprecated\u001b[39m q@1.1.2: You or someone you depend on is using Q, the JavaScript Promise library that gave Jav\u001b[38;60HaScript developers strong feelings about promises. They can almost certainly migrate to the native JavaScript prom\u001b[39;60Hise now. Thank you literally everyone for joining me in this bet against the odds. Be excellent to each other.\u001b[K\u001b[1m\u001b[40;60Hnpm\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[33mwarn\u001b[39m \u001b[94mdeprecated\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[1m\u001b[41;60Hnpm\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[33mwarn\u001b[39m \u001b[94mdeprecated\u001b[39m (For a CapTP with native promises, see @endo/eventual-send and @endo/captp)\u001b[K\u001b[1m\u001b[42;60Hnpm\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[33mwarn\u001b[39m \u001b[94mdeprecated\u001b[39m glob@4.2.2: Old versions of glob are not supported, and contain widely publicized security vul\u001b[43;60Hnerabilities, which have been fixed in the current version. Please update. Support for old versions may be purchas\u001b[44;60Hed (at exorbitant rates) by contac"]
